@import copy from '../../components/copy.tscl'
@import docs from '../../layouts/docs.tscl'
@import callout from '../../components/callout.tscl'

<docs [title]="'Rendering modes'" [path]="'/guide/rendering-modes'" [description]="'Choose per route whether a page is prerendered at build time or rendered on every request.'">
  <h1>Rendering modes</h1>
  <p class="lead">Each route chooses when it renders. The default is at build time; routes that depend on the request render on the server instead.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Renders</th><th><code>load()</code> runs</th><th>Good for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>static</code></td><td>once, at build, to an HTML file</td><td>once per page, at build</td><td>docs, blogs, marketing pages</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>server</code></td><td>on every request, by the server</td><td>on every request, with the request</td><td>accounts, search, anything per visitor</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Choosing a mode</h2>
  <p>List the routes that aren't static in the plugin options. A folder pattern such as <code>/account/*</code> covers the folder and everything under it; the most specific pattern wins.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre><code verbatim>// vite.config.ts
clarusjs({
  routes: {
    '/account/*': 'server',
    '/account/help': 'static',
  },
})</code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>

  <h2>Server routes</h2>
  <p>A server route is never prerendered, so a dynamic one needs no <code>entries()</code>. Its <code>load()</code> gets the visitor's <code>request</code>, for cookies, headers or query parameters.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre><code verbatim>// src/pages/account/[id].load.ts
export async function load({ params, request }) {
  const session = await getSession(request.headers.get('cookie'))
  return { account: await findAccount(params.id, session) }
}</code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <p><code>vite build</code> writes static routes to <code>dist/client</code> and leaves server routes to the handler in <code>dist/server/index.mjs</code>, a <code>fetch(Request)</code> function. <code>vite preview</code> serves both, and <code>clarusjs explain</code> shows each route's mode.</p>
  <callout [type]="'info'"><p>Every route on this site is static. Deploying server routes to Netlify Functions, and a client mode rendered in the browser, are the next steps on the roadmap.</p></callout>
</docs>
